            <![CDATA[
			<blockquote>
			<p>Microsoft researchers are urging travelers to assume that public and guest wireless networks at hotels, conference centers, and airports are untrustworthy. Whenever possible, users should rely on private connections, such as mobile hotspots and cellular data, instead of logging onto public wifi.</p>
			</blockquote>
			
			<p>This is good advice for everyone, not just travelers. </p>
			
			<p><a href="https://lifehacker.com/tech/heres-why-microsoft-is-encouraging-users-to-stay-off-public-wifi-networks">Source</a></p>
